IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `mc97-nouns`
IMPORT `mc97-c09`

-- TESTS for mc97-c09.l4. Every expected value is written from the text of chapter IX (extract line 32), before the run.

§ `Tests: chapter 9`

§§ `What each community shall have, in the text's words`

-- "The City of London shall have all the old Liberties and Customs [which it hath been used to have]."
#ASSERT `chapter 9: what the community shall have` `the City of London` EQUALS `all the old Liberties and Customs which it hath been used to have`
-- "all other Cities, Boroughs, Towns, and the Barons of the Five Ports, and all other Ports, shall have all their Liberties and free Customs."
#ASSERT `chapter 9: what the community shall have` `another City` EQUALS `all their Liberties and free Customs`
#ASSERT `chapter 9: what the community shall have` `a Borough` EQUALS `all their Liberties and free Customs`
#ASSERT `chapter 9: what the community shall have` `a Town` EQUALS `all their Liberties and free Customs`
#ASSERT `chapter 9: what the community shall have` `a Baron of the Five Ports` EQUALS `all their Liberties and free Customs`
#ASSERT `chapter 9: what the community shall have` `another Port` EQUALS `all their Liberties and free Customs`
-- A community of any other kind is not named.
#ASSERT `chapter 9: what the community shall have` `a community of another kind` EQUALS `not covered by chapter 9`

§§ `First sentence: the City of London keeps what is old AND what it hath been used to have`

#ASSERT `chapter 9, first sentence: the City of London shall have` `the City of London` TRUE TRUE EQUALS `covered by the text`
-- Old but not one it hath been used to have: the bracketed limb fails, so the text is silent.
#ASSERT `chapter 9, first sentence: the City of London shall have` `the City of London` TRUE FALSE EQUALS `not covered by the text`
-- One it hath been used to have but not old: the other limb fails.
#ASSERT `chapter 9, first sentence: the City of London shall have` `the City of London` FALSE TRUE EQUALS `not covered by the text`
#ASSERT `chapter 9, first sentence: the City of London shall have` `the City of London` FALSE FALSE EQUALS `not covered by the text`
-- The first sentence speaks only of the City of London.
#ASSERT `chapter 9, first sentence: the City of London shall have` `a Borough` TRUE TRUE EQUALS `not covered by the text`

§§ `Second sentence: the other communities keep their own Liberties and their own free Customs`

-- A Liberty of a Borough, its own: covered; "free" is not asked of a Liberty.
#ASSERT `chapter 9, second sentence: the other communities shall have` `a Borough` `a Liberty` TRUE FALSE EQUALS `covered by the text`
#ASSERT `chapter 9, second sentence: the other communities shall have` `a Borough` `a Liberty` TRUE TRUE EQUALS `covered by the text`
-- A Custom of a Borough, its own: covered only if free.
#ASSERT `chapter 9, second sentence: the other communities shall have` `a Borough` `a Custom` TRUE TRUE EQUALS `covered by the text`
#ASSERT `chapter 9, second sentence: the other communities shall have` `a Borough` `a Custom` TRUE FALSE EQUALS `not covered by the text`
-- Not the community's own: "their" is not met.
#ASSERT `chapter 9, second sentence: the other communities shall have` `a Borough` `a Liberty` FALSE TRUE EQUALS `not covered by the text`
-- Each named community, one case each.
#ASSERT `chapter 9, second sentence: the other communities shall have` `another City` `a Custom` TRUE TRUE EQUALS `covered by the text`
#ASSERT `chapter 9, second sentence: the other communities shall have` `a Town` `a Liberty` TRUE FALSE EQUALS `covered by the text`
#ASSERT `chapter 9, second sentence: the other communities shall have` `a Baron of the Five Ports` `a Custom` TRUE TRUE EQUALS `covered by the text`
#ASSERT `chapter 9, second sentence: the other communities shall have` `another Port` `a Liberty` TRUE TRUE EQUALS `covered by the text`
-- The City of London is not one of the "other" communities of the second sentence; nor is a community of another kind.
#ASSERT `chapter 9, second sentence: the other communities shall have` `the City of London` `a Liberty` TRUE TRUE EQUALS `not covered by the text`
#ASSERT `chapter 9, second sentence: the other communities shall have` `a community of another kind` `a Liberty` TRUE TRUE EQUALS `not covered by the text`

§§ `Both sentences together`

-- Arguments: community, thing, old, hath been used to have, own, free.
-- The City: the first sentence governs; the kind of thing, "own" and "free" are not asked.
#ASSERT `chapter 9: the community keeps the Liberty or Custom` `the City of London` `a Custom` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `covered by the text`
#ASSERT `chapter 9: the community keeps the Liberty or Custom` `the City of London` `a Liberty` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS `not covered by the text`
-- Another City: the second sentence governs; "old" and "used" are not asked.
#ASSERT `chapter 9: the community keeps the Liberty or Custom` `another City` `a Custom` FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS `covered by the text`
#ASSERT `chapter 9: the community keeps the Liberty or Custom` `another City` `a Custom` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `not covered by the text`
#ASSERT `chapter 9: the community keeps the Liberty or Custom` `a community of another kind` `a Liberty` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS `not covered by the text`

§§ `Who is to give effect`

-- "shall have" is in the passive in both sentences and names no one: NOTHING, not a guess.
#ASSERT `chapter 9: the party the text names to give effect to the entitlements` EQUALS NOTHING
